# LAB AND DECK CONTENT — authored prose, not source code.
#
# Prettier rewrites markdown constructs it considers equivalent, and slide
# markdown has load-bearing syntax it knows nothing about. The concrete case that
# forced this: Prettier normalizes `***` and `___` to `---`, and `---` is the
# SLIDE SEPARATOR — so a formatting pass could silently split one slide into two.
#
# The syntax this repo actually uses (HTML-comment config, `<!-- region -->`,
# `:::` directives) survives Prettier today, but relying on that is a standing
# bet on an external formatter's opinions about someone else's content. Authors
# in their own repos never run our Prettier anyway, so formatting here bought
# consistency we can't enforce in exchange for a risk we can't see.
